[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi! New contributor, aiming for a first PR to <code>Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/Reproducing.lean</code>. I'd like to add the bounded-point-evaluation bound:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_apply_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√‖</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It doesn't seem to be on master (the file has the matrix bound <code>norm_kernel_le</code>, not the element-wise one), and it's the \"bounded point evaluations\" fact that <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a> builds on. Short proof working locally.</p>\n<p>Is this wanted as a standalone lemma, or already covered/planned (e.g. in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a>)? Any naming preference?</p>\n<p>cc <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"983090\">@Tjeerd Jan Heeringa</span></p>",
        "id": 606952769,
        "sender_full_name": "Hao Zhang",
        "timestamp": 1782610833
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't know more about RKHS than there is in mathlib. Let me ask <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"871498\">@Hampus Nyberg</span></p>",
        "id": 606964235,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1782623578
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would say it is good to add; I would probably have made a PR for it after <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a> had been merged.</p>",
        "id": 606980848,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1782642044
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If your PR depends on the <code>eval</code> being explicit like in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a>, I can split that part of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a> into a separate PR.</p>",
        "id": 606981228,
        "sender_full_name": "Tjeerd Jan Heeringa",
        "timestamp": 1782642492
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree, it's definitely a lemma we want to have. Not sure about the naming, maybe just <code>norm_eval_le</code>?</p>",
        "id": 606984054,
        "sender_full_name": "Hampus Nyberg",
        "timestamp": 1782646115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I like <code>norm_eval_le</code> as well, it's may more descriptive imo</p>",
        "id": 606984228,
        "sender_full_name": "Amlal El Mahrouss",
        "timestamp": 1782646280
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks all! Going with <code>norm_eval_le</code>. Since the statement is on <code>f x</code> (like the existing <code>continuous_eval</code>), it doesn't need the explicit <code>eval</code> from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a> — so no need to split that out, Tjeerd, but thanks for offering.</p>\n<p>Here's the proof I have locally (compiles against current master's API), in case anyone wants to flag non-idiomatic bits before I open the PR:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_eval_le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√‖</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√‖</span><span class=\"n\">kernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_kerFun_eq_sqrt_norm_kernel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hsq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟪</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"n\">_𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟪</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"n\">_𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">inner_kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">calc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike.re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟪</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"n\">_𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">inner_self_eq_norm_sq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike.re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟪</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"n\">_𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖⟪</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟫</span><span class=\"n\">_𝕜</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">RCLike.re_le_norm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">norm_inner_le_norm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">gcongr</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le_opNorm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">‖</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ring</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nlinarith</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">norm_nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">norm_nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">norm_nonneg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">kerFun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hsq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I'll open a PR shortly unless someone sees a cleaner route.</p>",
