    {
        "content": "<p>PR is up: <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41129\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41129</a></p>\n<p>Adds <code>norm_eval_le</code> as discussed — stated on <code>f x</code>, so no dependency on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/37666\">#37666</a>. Thanks <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"871498\">@Hampus Nyberg</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1094358\">@Amlal El Mahrouss</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"983090\">@Tjeerd Jan Heeringa</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> for the naming and feedback!</p>",
        "id": 607005750,
        "sender_full_name": "Hao Zhang",
        "timestamp": 1782667630
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Update on <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41129\">#41129</a>: addressed <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span>'s review — golfed <code>norm_eval_le</code> to a <code>grw</code>/adjoint proof, reworded the docstring so it doesn't read as a uniform bound, and factored out <code>adjoint_kerFun</code> (<code>(kerFun H x).adjoint f = f x</code>). CI is green. Ready for another look whenever — thanks!</p>",
        "id": 607013726,
        "sender_full_name": "Hao Zhang",
